<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <fullName>Attachment_Status__c</fullName>
    <description>Work-queue status of this row's attachment carrier (v2 persistence redesign, 2026-08-06 — see design-requirements-attachment-persistence-v2.md §6.4/§10.2 A1). Required to exist, not optional — AttachmentCarrierSweepBatch selects on this field to find rows with retry work outstanding, and a Long Text notes field cannot serve as a work queue. Stamped None/Pending by the synchronous handler at staging-row creation, then advanced to Saved/Partial/Failed/Not Saved/Expired by AttachmentPersistQueueable, AttachmentPersistFinalizer, or AttachmentCarrierSweepBatch as the carrier moves through conversion, deferral, retry, or expiry.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Pending = carrier written, not yet converted. Saved = all files converted, carrier removed. Partial = some files converted, remainder still on the carrier and will retry. Failed = the file job died; the carrier is intact and will retry. Not Saved = the carrier itself was never written, or the email was gated/a duplicate delivery — there is nothing to retry. Expired = unconverted for 14+ days; carrier removed by the sweeper.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Attachment Status</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <type>Picklist</type>
    <!--
      RESTRICTED PICKLIST, VERIFIED 2026-08-06: of the seven values below, ONLY Not_Saved has a
      fullName that differs from its label (fullName Not_Saved, label "Not Saved"). None, Pending,
      Saved, Partial, Failed and Expired all have fullName identical to label, so this trap is
      confined to the one value.

      Apex binds to the fullName (the API name), not the label, because this value set is
      restricted: writing the label text "Not Saved" instead of the API name Not_Saved throws
      INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST at runtime, with nothing to catch it at compile time.

      InboundEmailStagingService.cls is the SOLE OWNER of this binding
      (ATTACHMENT_STATUS_NOT_SAVED = 'Not_Saved', with an underscore); every other class that
      touches this value (InboundEmailAttachmentService, AttachmentCarrierSweepBatch,
      AttachmentPersistQueueable, AttachmentPersistFinalizer, ExtractAddressQueueable,
      EmailToLeadHandler, InboundEmailStagingSelector) is a CONSUMER of that constant, not a second
      place where the literal is defined. If this value set is ever re-cut, update the constant in
      InboundEmailStagingService.cls in the same change; do not edit any consumer class instead.
    -->
    <valueSet>
        <restricted>true</restricted>
        <valueSetDefinition>
            <sorted>false</sorted>
            <value>
                <fullName>None</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>None</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Pending</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Pending</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Saved</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Saved</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Partial</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Partial</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Failed</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Failed</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Not_Saved</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Not Saved</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Expired</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Expired</label>
            </value>
        </valueSetDefinition>
    </valueSet>
</CustomField>
